# Research pipeline brief (2026-07-30): per-job override for agent_propose.sh
# (AGENT_JOB_OVERRIDES). Non-secret task wiring only — API keys stay in the canonical
# secrets.env, sourced first.
#
# EXAMPLE ONLY. The live file lives OUTSIDE git at
#   ~/.config/agent-workforce/knowledge_digest.env  (mode 600, owned by dave)
# and is intentionally NOT committed — mirrors m1_signal_scan.env exactly.
# Install: copy the vars below into that path, then chmod 600.
#
# Why this exists: Mechanism C of the research pipeline brief — a weekly report of what
# the *knowledge base* learned (git-log delta over 05_knowledge/ and 11_entities/),
# distinct from the existing *activity* digest (weekly-pre-assembly, daily-logs/Notion/
# open-loops driven). Runs headless Claude Code (Opus 5, box subscription, $0 OpenRouter
# spend) and refuses to run at all (bin/vault_sync_guard.sh check) rather than digest off
# a stale or dirty mirror.
AGENT_PROFILE=claude-opus
# AGENT_OWNER is the PERSONA that owns this workflow in design/agents/<name>.toml.
# It keys the episodic memory store (~/.hermes/profiles/$AGENT_OWNER/memories) and is
# deliberately NOT the same field as AGENT_PROFILE, which names the RUNTIME and keys
# cost.log's profile= column. Merging them is what made this job log memory=no-store on
# every run: there is no ~/.hermes/profiles/claude-opus/. (W1, 2026-09-02.)
AGENT_OWNER=claudius
AGENT_TASK_SLUG=knowledge-digest
# Optional: cap retries so a transient failure doesn't triple-run an expensive Claude
# Code pass (default is 3).
AGENT_MAX_ATTEMPTS=2
AGENT_RUNTIME_CMD='~/agent-workforce/bin/run_knowledge_digest_cc.sh'
AGENT_VERIFY_CMD='~/agent-workforce/bin/proposal_or_decline.sh knowledge-digest'
